    <bpmn:startEvent id="START" name="Demand raised on the Single Front Door"/>
    <bpmn:task id="IN_01" name="IN-01 Complete Required Demand Submission Information">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 1. Business need, request type, impacted markets, sponsor, required date, initial effort, funding position, dependencies and supporting evidence. Team: Requestor. Tool: Single Front Door (Pega). Status: I. Confidence: provisional (Single Front Door, DAM triage and Demand Board detail follows the booklet; the independent WS4 original is not established, so nothing here is C1 or C2 until it is.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IN_02" name="IN-02 Raise Demand on Single Front Door">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 1. Submit the demand on the Single Front Door (G0); merges OFF-011 and DM-01. Team: Requestor. Tool: Single Front Door (Pega). Output: G0. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (Single Front Door, DAM triage and Demand Board detail follows the booklet; the independent WS4 original is not established, so nothing here is C1 or C2 until it is.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IN_03" name="IN-03 Generate Demand Reference">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 1. Register the demand for tracking. Team: Demand Assurance Manager (DAM). Tool: Pega. Output: Demand reference. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (Single Front Door, DAM triage and Demand Board detail follows the booklet; the independent WS4 original is not established, so nothing here is C1 or C2 until it is.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IN_04" name="IN-04 DAM Completeness Check">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 1. Check that the submission is complete. Team: Demand Assurance Manager (DAM). Tool: Pega. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (Single Front Door, DAM triage and Demand Board detail follows the booklet; the independent WS4 original is not established, so nothing here is C1 or C2 until it is.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_13" name="Demand complete?"/>
    <bpmn:task id="IN_05" name="IN-05 DAM Triage and Classification">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 1. Triage the demand and confirm its classification and route; merges OFF-013, OFF-014 and DM-02. Team: Demand Assurance Manager (DAM). Tool: Pega. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (Single Front Door, DAM triage and Demand Board detail follows the booklet; the independent WS4 original is not established, so nothing here is C1 or C2 until it is.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IN_06" name="IN-06 Identify Impacted Functions">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 1. Identify the impacted NW functions and verticals. Team: Demand Assurance Manager (DAM). Tool: Pega. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (Single Front Door, DAM triage and Demand Board detail follows the booklet; the independent WS4 original is not established, so nothing here is C1 or C2 until it is.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_14" name="Cross-functional?"/>
    <bpmn:task id="IN_07" name="IN-07 Cross-functional Handshake">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 1. Handshake with other NW function PS or vertical SPOC for cross-functional demand. Team: NW Vertical Function SPOC. Tool: . Status: I. Confidence: provisional (Single Front Door, DAM triage and Demand Board detail follows the booklet; the independent WS4 original is not established, so nothing here is C1 or C2 until it is.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Triage_outcome" name="Triage outcome?"/>
    <bpmn:task id="FA.01.01" name="FA.01.01 Accept Request and Initiate EDM Allocation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Accept the request and initiate EDM allocation. Team: Market Delivery Manager (MDM). Tool: . Status: C1. Confidence: supported (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="FA.01.02" name="FA.01.02 EDM Appointment">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Appoint the Engineering Delivery Manager. Team: Market Delivery Manager (MDM). Tool: . Status: C1. Confidence: supported (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="FA.02.01" name="FA.02.01 Team and Solution Authority Allocation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Allocate the delivery team and the Solution Authority. Team: Engineering Delivery Manager (EDM). Tool: . Status: C1. Confidence: supported (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IA_01" name="IA-01 Functional Impact Assessment">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. NW vertical teams and other NW functions assess impact (from DM-05, DM-06). Team: Team in NSE Vertical. Tool: . Status: I. Confidence: provisional (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IA_02" name="IA-02 IT Impact Assessment">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. IT assesses impact where IT dependencies exist (from DM-07). Team: IT. Tool: . Status: I. Confidence: provisional (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IA_03" name="IA-03 Technical Feasibility and HLD">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Technical feasibility, high-level design or solution definition (from DM-08, DM-10). Team: Solution Authority. Tool: . Status: I. Confidence: provisional (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="FA.03.xx" name="FA.03.xx Security, Privacy, Resilience and Operations Impact">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Security, privacy, resilience and operations-impact activities. Team: Team in NSE Vertical. Tool: . Status: C1. Confidence: supported (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="FA.04.xx" name="FA.04.xx Feasibility Analysis and Cost Estimation">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Feasibility analysis and cost estimation. Team: Solution Authority. Tool: . Status: C1. Confidence: supported (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IA_04" name="IA-04 Resource Estimate">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Estimate delivery resources; WFM detail not evidenced. Team: Engineering Delivery Manager (EDM). Tool: WFM. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IA_05" name="IA-05 Budget and Priority Check">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Check budget availability and priority with the market sponsor and NSE Planning (from DM-12, DM-13). Team: Demand Governance Team. Tool: . Status: I. Confidence: provisional (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="IA_06" name="IA-06 Consolidated Impact Assessment">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 2. Consolidate the impact assessment; for in-year demand, submit it to the Demand Board (from DM-14). Team: Demand Governance Team. Tool: . Output: G2 submission. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (FA activities and sequence are C1 against NSE E2E Project Delivery Process_2025 and RACI; local role variations require market confirmation. Impact-assessment steps that depend on the WS4 demand process are I until an independently authored WS4 source is established.)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="DM_15" name="DM-15 Demand Board Decision">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 3. The Demand Board reviews the consolidated impact assessment and decides. Team: Demand Governance Team. Tool: . Output: Approval or rejection. Status: I. Confidence: provisional (NCAR, NPRB and market routes are conditional (V), not consecutive steps; entry criteria and thresholds are not confirmed. Demand Board detail depends on the WS4 source (I).)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_15" name="Demand Board approved?"/>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="GW_16" name="Does the demand change the approved in-year plan?"/>
    <bpmn:task id="DM_17" name="DM-17 NCAR In-year Change Route">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 3. NCAR governs approval of changes to the in-year plan, including agreement on prioritisation. Team: Demand Governance Team. Tool: . Output: NCAR decision. Status: V. Confidence: supported (NCAR, NPRB and market routes are conditional (V), not consecutive steps; entry criteria and thresholds are not confirmed. Demand Board detail depends on the WS4 source (I).)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="NPRB_check" name="Requires project or funding mobilisation through NPRB?"/>
    <bpmn:task id="DM_19" name="DM-19 NPRB Route">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 3. NPRB manages project and funding mobilisation for the in-year project. Team: Demand Governance Team. Tool: . Output: NPRB decision. Status: V. Confidence: supported (NCAR, NPRB and market routes are conditional (V), not consecutive steps; entry criteria and thresholds are not confirmed. Demand Board detail depends on the WS4 source (I).)</bpmn:documentation>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Market_check" name="Another market-specific approval applies?"/>
    <bpmn:task id="DM_24" name="DM-24 Documented Market Governance Route">
      <bpmn:documentation>Phase 3. Follow the market's documented governance route. Team: Market governance (per market). Tool: . Status: V. Confidence: supported (NCAR, NPRB and market routes are conditional (V), not consecutive steps; entry criteria and thresholds are not confirmed. Demand Board detail depends on the WS4 source (I).)</bpmn:documentation>
